    "text": "London gains young adults and loses everyone else; rural regions do the reverse",
    "subtitle": [
      "Net internal migration (moves in minus moves out, within the UK) as % of each age group's population a year, pooled 2012\u201324.",
      "England and Wales: London, then the other 30 ITL2 regions in thirds by population-weighted density. International migration excluded.",
      "Sources: ONS internal migration estimates (England and Wales); ONS mid-year population estimates; ONS Longitudinal Business Database; authors' calculations."
    ]
